WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.638 --> 00:00:03.710
Today we talk about acrylic nails.

00:00:03.956 --> 00:00:08.272
It is a way of doing extensions that has been around for a very long time,

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:09.310
it is very strong,

00:00:09.579 --> 00:00:11.550
and many clients still choose it today.

00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:14.590
But acrylic does not forgive careless work.

00:00:14.939 --> 00:00:19.773
The wrong ratio, the wrong structure, or product touching the skin,

00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:21.630
and the nails lift, break,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.110
and sometimes the client develops an allergy.

00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:26.519
First, how does acrylic work?

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:28.439
The system has two parts.

00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:32.039
The liquid part, which in the trade we simply call the liquid.

00:00:32.308 --> 00:00:33.159
And the powder.

00:00:33.644 --> 00:00:37.061
When a brush wet with liquid touches the powder, the two mix,

00:00:37.011 --> 00:00:39.159
and the reaction starts straight away,

00:00:39.279 --> 00:00:40.119
in the open air.

00:00:40.369 --> 00:00:41.399
No lamp needed.

00:00:41.748 --> 00:00:45.799
In just a few minutes, the soft bead hardens into a solid mass.

00:00:46.093 --> 00:00:49.319
So the time you have to place and shape the bead is very short.

00:00:49.484 --> 00:00:52.119
Your hand has to be steady, and decisive.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.770
The most important thing in acrylic work is the ratio of liquid to powder.

00:00:57.187 --> 00:01:00.370
A correct bead is moist, glossy and round.

00:01:00.805 --> 00:01:05.247
Placed on the nail, it holds its shape, then slowly spreads out a little,

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:06.450
but it does not run.

00:01:07.106 --> 00:01:11.208
Each brand has its own ratio, so read the instructions of the brand,

00:01:11.158 --> 00:01:13.890
and train your hand, first on practice nails,

00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:15.570
and only then on clients.

00:01:16.135 --> 00:01:19.888
A bead that is too wet has a lot of liquid and too little powder.

00:01:20.144 --> 00:01:25.311
It runs, floods into the side corners and the cuticle area, sets slowly,

00:01:25.261 --> 00:01:27.088
and once set, it is weak.

00:01:27.492 --> 00:01:28.210
Worse still,

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.608
excess liquid that has not fully reacted can collect on the skin of the client.

00:01:32.945 --> 00:01:34.528
That is one road to allergy.

00:01:35.186 --> 00:01:37.497
A bead that is too dry is the opposite.

00:01:37.906 --> 00:01:42.537
The surface is rough, with tiny pinholes, and the edge of the tip is crumbly.

00:01:43.043 --> 00:01:45.853
Dry acrylic bonds poorly and lifts easily,

00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:49.337
and a porous surface picks up dirt and stains easily.

00:01:49.864 --> 00:01:53.337
To know whether your hand is right, look at the surface you just shaped:

00:01:53.443 --> 00:01:57.897
smooth, moist and glossy, with no holes, means it is right.

00:01:58.557 --> 00:02:01.232
As for structure, acrylic is just like builder gel,

00:02:01.182 --> 00:02:03.496
which you learned in the builder gel lesson.

00:02:03.912 --> 00:02:05.496
Thin right at the cuticle.

00:02:05.787 --> 00:02:06.776
Thin at the tip.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:10.434
And thickest at the apex, which sits over the stress area,

00:02:10.384 --> 00:02:12.456
where the nail leaves the skin bed,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.896
slightly towards the back.

00:02:14.377 --> 00:02:17.925
Seen from the tip, the C curve must be even on both sides,

00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:20.216
with the side walls straight and neat.

00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:22.936
With extensions, this matters even more.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.496
The longer the extension, the greater the force bending the nail every day.

00:02:28.117 --> 00:02:30.859
Whether acrylic bonds well is decided in the prep.

00:02:31.271 --> 00:02:33.099
Dry prep, no soaking.

00:02:33.522 --> 00:02:34.802
Push back the cuticle,

00:02:34.752 --> 00:02:38.379
and remove the thin layer of skin still stuck to the nail plate.

00:02:38.904 --> 00:02:42.859
Buff lightly to remove the shine, then clean off the dust and oil.

00:02:43.197 --> 00:02:44.379
Then comes primer.

00:02:44.802 --> 00:02:47.419
There are acid primers and acid free primers.

00:02:47.592 --> 00:02:51.514
Either way, apply a very thin layer, on the nail plate only,

00:02:51.464 --> 00:02:53.579
and never let it touch the skin,

00:02:53.768 --> 00:02:55.019
because it can burn the skin.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.065
Which one to use, how to apply it, and how long to let it dry,

00:02:59.015 --> 00:03:02.779
all follow the instructions of the acrylic brand you are using.

00:03:03.399 --> 00:03:05.196
There is something that happens a lot:

00:03:05.466 --> 00:03:09.676
the client comes back after a week, and the acrylic has lifted at the cuticle.

00:03:10.004 --> 00:03:12.156
The reason is usually one of a few things:

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:14.636
the nail was not prepped thoroughly.

00:03:14.889 --> 00:03:17.116
Too little primer, or too much.

00:03:17.503 --> 00:03:20.396
Acrylic touching the skin, flooding the corners.

00:03:20.905 --> 00:03:22.796
The edge at the cuticle too thick.

00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:24.396
A bead that was too dry.

00:03:24.741 --> 00:03:28.076
Or no apex, so the nail is bent every day.

00:03:28.312 --> 00:03:30.796
When you see lifting, do not build over it.

00:03:31.041 --> 00:03:33.836
Water and dirt can be trapped under the lifted part.

00:03:34.185 --> 00:03:37.756
File the lifted part away, and only then do the infill.

00:03:38.278 --> 00:03:39.596
Now, safety.

00:03:39.923 --> 00:03:44.556
The liquid has a very strong smell, evaporates fast, and is flammable.

00:03:44.977 --> 00:03:48.556
In Helsinki, the hygiene guidance of the city states clearly:

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.474
where acrylic nails are done,

00:03:50.424 --> 00:03:53.996
the workstation must have an efficient enough local exhaust system.

00:03:54.345 --> 00:03:58.327
And when filing creates dust, that too must be extracted at the source,

00:03:58.277 --> 00:04:00.876
so the dust does not spread through the salon.

00:04:01.118 --> 00:04:04.716
Rules differ from country to country, and from city to city.

00:04:05.054 --> 00:04:06.556
But the principle is the same:

00:04:06.736 --> 00:04:11.116
extract right where the vapor and dust are made, and wear a mask when filing.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.000
A few more small habits that are well worth it.

00:04:14.531 --> 00:04:19.096
Pour very little liquid, just enough for one client, into a small covered dish,

00:04:19.046 --> 00:04:21.840
and close the lid whenever you are not using it.

00:04:22.426 --> 00:04:24.320
Close the big bottle straight away.

00:04:24.702 --> 00:04:27.040
Keep it away from flames and heat sources.

00:04:27.388 --> 00:04:29.600
Leftover liquid does not go down the sink.

00:04:30.028 --> 00:04:33.027
Dispose of it according to the safety data sheet of the product,

00:04:32.977 --> 00:04:34.640
and the waste rules where you work.

00:04:34.872 --> 00:04:37.840
Paper towels soaked with liquid go in a bin with a lid.

00:04:38.495 --> 00:04:39.927
One more thing about liquid.

00:04:40.251 --> 00:04:42.087
Some liquids are made with MMA.

00:04:42.498 --> 00:04:44.842
In the United States, back in the 1970s,

00:04:44.792 --> 00:04:50.807
the Food and Drug Administration had products made entirely of this substance withdrawn from the market,

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:53.687
after many cases of damaged nails and skin.

00:04:54.184 --> 00:04:54.894
In Germany,

00:04:54.844 --> 00:05:01.127
the federal institute for risk assessment advises manufacturers not to use it in nail modeling products.

00:05:01.299 --> 00:05:05.207
Liquids for professionals usually use a different substance, such as EMA.

00:05:05.576 --> 00:05:09.045
So only buy products with a clear label and a safety data sheet,

00:05:08.995 --> 00:05:10.327
from a trusted supplier.

00:05:10.584 --> 00:05:13.527
Do not be tempted by cheap products of unknown origin.

00:05:14.126 --> 00:05:17.936
For more on allergy, review the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:05:18.301 --> 00:05:21.136
Here, you only need to remember one sentence:

00:05:21.245 --> 00:05:23.950
liquid, and acrylic that has not yet hardened,

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:27.296
must never touch the skin of the client, or your own skin.

00:05:27.932 --> 00:05:29.389
Then there are infills.

00:05:29.561 --> 00:05:33.289
As the nail grows out, the acrylic slowly moves towards the tip,

00:05:33.239 --> 00:05:34.669
taking the apex with it.

00:05:35.174 --> 00:05:38.829
The nail becomes top heavy, and breaks and lifts more easily.

00:05:39.255 --> 00:05:43.069
Usually every two to three weeks, the client should come back for an infill.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.829
And be honest with the client:

00:05:45.104 --> 00:05:49.789
acrylic is very strong, but the natural nail underneath still needs gentle care.

00:05:50.111 --> 00:05:55.229
Do not pick at it, and do not use your nails as tools to pry or to open things.

00:05:55.823 --> 00:05:57.241
As for removing acrylic.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:01.401
Acrylic dissolves in acetone, but it takes quite a bit longer than gel.

00:06:01.829 --> 00:06:05.055
File the acrylic thinner first, then soak it in acetone,

00:06:05.005 --> 00:06:07.721
and only push off the parts that have softened,

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:08.521
gently.

00:06:08.949 --> 00:06:11.401
Never pry, and never snap it off.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:14.121
The steps are the same as in the gel removal lesson;

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.641
it just takes more patience.

00:06:16.259 --> 00:06:19.089
You see, acrylic is not hard for the hands.

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:20.529
It is hard for the head:

00:06:20.775 --> 00:06:25.089
the right ratio, the right structure, and keeping the product off the skin.

00:06:25.428 --> 00:06:27.889
Once you understand it, your hands will follow.

00:06:28.144 --> 00:06:31.249
In the practice lesson, we will go step by step together.

00:06:31.449 --> 00:06:34.049
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:35.089
See you next time.
